 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. NBX-PUT-NUMS.
*> USING compound, key (PIC X(16)), element type, count (1 to 3), a, b, c (FLOAT-LONG): a list of that many numbers set in the compound.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-T-LIST              BINARY-LONG VALUE 9.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ZERO-D              FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-LIST                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INT                 BINARY-DOUBLE.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-COMPOUND             BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-KEY                  PIC X(16).
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-COUNT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-A                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-B                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-C                    FLOAT-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-COMPOUND L-KEY L-TYPE L-COUNT L-A L-B L-C.
     CALL "NBX-PUT-N" USING L-COMPOUND L-KEY WS-T-LIST WS-ZERO WS-ZERO-D WS-LIST
     CALL "NBX-ELEM" USING WS-LIST L-TYPE WS-ZERO L-A
     CALL "NBX-ELEM" USING WS-LIST L-TYPE WS-ZERO L-B
     IF L-COUNT = 3
         CALL "NBX-ELEM" USING WS-LIST L-TYPE WS-ZERO L-C
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM NBX-PUT-NUMS.
